findings.body:
**Move the enrollment enqueue after the dispatch recheck.**

`src/ops/review/addressMany.ts:413` sends the durable queue enqueue before three later steps:
- isolation (Line 424)
- the isolated-repo identity check (Line 441)
- the eligibility and head recheck (Lines 443-458)

The enqueue therefore runs even when those steps fail. If the PR head moves, the PR becomes a draft or closes, or isolation refuses, the queue still holds an entry. The row then reports `enrollment: { state: 'enrolled' }` while the leg is `needs-human` or `exception` and was never dispatched. A caller cannot see that the queue holds an entry for a leg the run refused.

Do the enqueue only after `revalidated` passes and before `address(...)`. On every refusal path, keep the default `requestedEnrollment(...)` value ("Requested but leg not dispatched").

<details>
<summary>Proposed reorder</summary>

```diff
-            if (request) {
-              try { ... enqueue ... } catch { ... }
-            }
             const root = deps.isolate
 ...
             } else {
+              if (request) {
+                try { ... enqueue ... } catch { ... }
+              }
               dispatched = true;
```
</details>
